WEBVTT

00:01.690 --> 00:02.710
My name is

00:03.320 --> 00:04.910
Kyotaro Ichikawa.

00:06.660 --> 00:07.740
Second year middle school student.

00:09.030 --> 00:10.620
Today, my third semester starts.

00:12.410 --> 00:15.180
This is... Anna Yamada.

00:15.710 --> 00:16.540
That's all.

00:17.920 --> 00:19.130
Oh!

00:19.250 --> 00:21.690
Ichikawa, you really did break a bone!

00:21.800 --> 00:23.650
Yamada told me about it...

00:23.650 --> 00:24.520
Hey, Chii...

00:24.520 --> 00:26.940
You fell at the snow mountain in Akita?

00:26.940 --> 00:27.690
Chii...

00:27.840 --> 00:30.200
- Somehow, I got surrounded.
- Let's write on his cast!

00:30.720 --> 00:32.030
- Chii!
- Like a message wall?

00:33.730 --> 00:35.870
Don't get too cocky just because
you have a bone broken!

00:36.230 --> 00:37.940
Don't say it like it's a good thing!

00:40.440 --> 00:41.460
What is this?

00:41.610 --> 00:42.540
Crap!

00:42.540 --> 00:43.690
Oh, no, that's...

00:44.110 --> 00:44.860
Gross.

00:46.110 --> 00:47.970
Trying some gap appeal?

00:48.490 --> 00:51.430
I think I might lose it,
so let's just put it away...

00:51.430 --> 00:52.120
Hey.

00:53.240 --> 00:55.370
If there's anything you're
having trouble with...

00:55.660 --> 00:56.710
Dayama!

00:57.540 --> 00:59.840
I brought you souvenirs from Osaka!

01:02.380 --> 01:03.270
Off I go!

02:42.480 --> 02:44.110
(Class 2-3)
How unfortunate.

02:44.410 --> 02:45.940
Must be inconvenient
since it's your dominant hand.

02:46.270 --> 02:47.920
No, I've gotten used to it.

02:48.900 --> 02:51.660
Isn't it easier to ask
someone else for help?

02:51.950 --> 02:53.700
No, well...

02:54.120 --> 02:57.720
This development is
one I'm the worst at...

02:57.720 --> 03:00.660
Who are you closest with in class?

03:00.870 --> 03:03.330
There it is! My closest classmate!

03:03.580 --> 03:04.790
Yamada?

03:05.250 --> 03:06.500
How about her?

03:06.500 --> 03:07.770
Her seat's also close to you.

03:08.230 --> 03:10.260
Y-Yamada...

03:10.670 --> 03:12.180
She has a lot of friends.

03:12.510 --> 03:13.470
And she's also busy.

03:14.180 --> 03:16.950
Y-Yamada is someone
I just talk to ocassionally.

03:16.950 --> 03:18.320
We're not close or anything.

03:18.640 --> 03:19.540
I see.

03:19.540 --> 03:20.620
Don't worry about it.

03:20.770 --> 03:24.560
I'll try to manage classes
and breaks with one hand...

03:31.190 --> 03:32.040
This is bad.

03:32.110 --> 03:33.090
This is bad, this is bad!

03:33.090 --> 03:35.570
Why did it become like this so suddenly?!

03:35.870 --> 03:41.160
We literally just... just finally became
a little bit closer over the winter!

03:41.930 --> 03:44.120
I made it all for naught.

03:44.250 --> 03:45.540
With my own hands!

03:48.690 --> 03:51.510
Using my left hand really is hard...

03:53.970 --> 03:56.760
No choice.
I have to ask someone to make a copy.

04:05.940 --> 04:07.460
Right! I'll ask Hara...

04:07.460 --> 04:08.750
No, I shouldn't!

04:08.750 --> 04:11.110
I think I absolutely shouldn't do that.

04:12.030 --> 04:12.820
Here you go.

04:14.200 --> 04:17.380
I really feel like I'm being relied on!

04:17.380 --> 04:18.410
By Yamada!

04:18.820 --> 04:19.790
Yamada?

04:20.580 --> 04:21.950
Make a copy of notes?

04:22.200 --> 04:24.120
Yeah, for Ichikawa.

04:24.410 --> 04:26.620
My handwriting is awful, so...

04:27.290 --> 04:28.130
That's what she said!

04:29.040 --> 04:33.270
"I can only ask someone
as kind and cool as Adachi for this!"

04:33.270 --> 04:35.020
She said that!

04:35.470 --> 04:37.700
She definitely didn't say that.

04:38.150 --> 04:40.060
S-She didn't... I guess...

04:52.120 --> 04:53.420
U-Um...

04:54.110 --> 04:54.990
I'm sorry.

04:56.650 --> 04:57.570
For what?

04:58.410 --> 05:00.570
For what I said to Teach.

05:01.120 --> 05:02.540
What you said to Teach...

05:03.040 --> 05:04.500
What was wrong with it?

05:05.330 --> 05:06.370
Say it.

05:07.000 --> 05:08.480
Uh, um...

05:08.960 --> 05:10.790
W-What was it again?

05:11.590 --> 05:13.560
Um, so you see, uh...

05:14.260 --> 05:18.510
I... felt bad having to...
get you to help me, so...

05:19.090 --> 05:19.890
But...

05:20.410 --> 05:23.510
You're actually the one I...
want to rely on the most.

05:24.140 --> 05:25.600
Actually.

05:28.730 --> 05:29.810
I know.

05:30.480 --> 05:33.400
Whaaaat?!

05:36.110 --> 05:38.170
You're not going home by car?

05:38.450 --> 05:41.200
My mom has her part-time job,
so I'm walking home.

05:41.380 --> 05:43.220
Then, I'll carry your bag for you!

05:43.220 --> 05:44.660
N-No, I...

05:47.910 --> 05:49.370
Then, if you would...

05:54.170 --> 05:57.110
Also, try not to talk to Adachi so much.

05:57.110 --> 05:57.970
Why's that?

05:57.970 --> 05:59.380
Why's that, huh?

06:00.720 --> 06:02.220
After that...

06:02.650 --> 06:05.410
Yamada started helping me out with things.

06:06.730 --> 06:08.600
I'll take your tray back with me.

06:08.940 --> 06:11.400
Huh?! I'm still sipping my soup...

06:12.310 --> 06:14.570
Which spoon... was mine?

06:14.860 --> 06:16.330
I-I-I'm sorry!

06:17.280 --> 06:18.940
What got you shaking?

06:18.940 --> 06:20.300
(Library)

06:20.300 --> 06:22.910
Three weeks passed with my cast on.

06:23.240 --> 06:25.630
I've gotten used to
my lack of freedom, but...

06:26.290 --> 06:27.140
N-Next.

06:36.210 --> 06:37.210
Catch!

06:40.760 --> 06:42.680
Sorry! I forgot...

06:43.390 --> 06:45.390
I'm not used to Yamada's way of helping.

06:46.060 --> 06:47.970
Hey, check this out.

06:47.970 --> 06:49.520
What is it? Porn mags?!

06:49.520 --> 06:50.440
Not quite.

06:50.440 --> 06:53.100
Whaat? Oh, it's an idol magazine.

06:53.100 --> 06:55.120
You really do like Lemonzaka46, huh?

06:55.120 --> 06:56.710
Come on, just take a look!

06:56.710 --> 06:59.340
Making so much ruckus
over a mere magazine...

06:59.340 --> 07:01.090
They still are lowlifes.

07:01.090 --> 07:03.300
Wooow! That's Yamada!

07:03.300 --> 07:03.990
Wha...

07:04.780 --> 07:07.090
Wow! So her stage name is Akino!

07:07.090 --> 07:09.830
But isn't Yamada a model?

07:10.370 --> 07:12.560
What, you don't even know?

07:13.310 --> 07:16.880
She's not just a model, but she
also does variety shows and movies!

07:16.880 --> 07:18.480
Her agency probably told her to do it.

07:21.590 --> 07:23.050
Crap! I did it...

07:23.610 --> 07:26.640
But the fact that she's in
an idol magazine means...

07:26.700 --> 07:29.120
The fact that she's in
an idol magazine means...

07:29.120 --> 07:31.850
Is she maybe trying to become an idol?

07:31.850 --> 07:33.200
Swimsuits?!

07:33.200 --> 07:35.660
Tch! We thought of the same thing!

07:35.660 --> 07:39.380
...whatever it is,
Yamada in a micro-biki...

07:41.400 --> 07:43.710
Yamada, p-please do a micro.

07:48.540 --> 07:49.160
Hey.

07:49.870 --> 07:51.870
What were you talking about
with Adachi today?

07:52.580 --> 07:53.920
I knew she'd ask.

07:54.600 --> 07:55.730
N-Nothing much.

07:56.330 --> 07:58.210
A boys conversation?

07:58.800 --> 07:59.750
Well...

08:00.250 --> 08:01.050
Sorry.

08:01.790 --> 08:02.860
Speaking of which,

08:03.130 --> 08:05.470
I wonder if I can ask her about work.

08:06.300 --> 08:10.430
I guess it didn't look like
a male-oriented gravure.

08:11.270 --> 08:13.640
Oh, right!
Can we stop by the convenience store?

08:16.060 --> 08:18.210
Oooh! Look!

08:18.210 --> 08:21.150
It's Honoka Saito from Lemonzaka46!

08:21.150 --> 08:22.570
So cute!

08:24.950 --> 08:25.820
Wha...

08:26.200 --> 08:28.340
T-This is...

08:28.990 --> 08:30.490
It's Yamada.

08:30.740 --> 08:32.830
Oh, the horoscopes.

08:33.160 --> 08:34.000
Hmph.

08:35.390 --> 08:38.130
This took way more time than usual.

08:38.540 --> 08:41.670
They told me to act natural,
so I got nervous.

08:41.980 --> 08:43.540
Doesn't look like you were, though.

08:43.760 --> 08:46.800
But the staff there was so funny!

08:46.800 --> 08:48.530
Ah, sorry!

08:48.760 --> 08:50.030
I guess it doesn't matter.

08:51.100 --> 08:53.430
Um, you're like your usual self,

08:53.730 --> 08:55.160
so I think it came out great.

08:55.430 --> 08:59.520
Uh, what I mean is,
your usual self is already the best you...

09:00.110 --> 09:02.110
The Yamada I'm used to seeing, I mean...

09:02.690 --> 09:04.110
Complimenting people is hard!

09:05.400 --> 09:06.450
I see.

09:07.150 --> 09:09.700
The me that you're used to seeing

09:10.280 --> 09:12.220
is the best version of me, you're saying?

09:12.450 --> 09:13.660
Why are you saying it like that?

09:14.040 --> 09:15.290
I mean...

09:16.160 --> 09:18.190
Nothing. Let me buy this for you.

09:21.480 --> 09:24.150
I switched the topic to anecdotes
about my broken arm, but...

09:24.630 --> 09:26.920
I'll ask her bit by bit.

09:27.550 --> 09:29.680
About her world that I don't know.

09:30.930 --> 09:32.050
Who do you like the most?

09:32.510 --> 09:34.070
No one in particular.

09:34.350 --> 09:36.020
So you like all of them!

09:37.140 --> 09:40.690
But you're completely different than
how you are in fashion magazines.

09:45.490 --> 09:46.790
You've seen it before?

09:46.790 --> 09:48.240
Huh? N-No, I...

09:48.610 --> 09:50.120
My sister bought it by coincidence.

09:51.320 --> 09:52.970
Oh, uh, I see!

09:53.970 --> 09:54.950
I guessed as much.

09:55.830 --> 09:56.870
It's so different!

09:57.120 --> 10:00.330
The makeup, the poses,
and the atmosphere of the shoot...

10:00.670 --> 10:01.920
I-I see.

10:02.170 --> 10:03.170
Also...

10:03.710 --> 10:05.920
You... like your job, huh?

10:09.760 --> 10:10.510
Yeah.

10:13.050 --> 10:15.720
I couldn't see
Yamada's smile with my own eyes.

10:16.430 --> 10:17.270
It's probably because...

10:17.770 --> 10:20.480
...the sun was too bright.

10:22.000 --> 10:23.790
(Home Ec Room)

10:24.980 --> 10:26.500
Ack!

10:26.610 --> 10:28.150
Break it gently.

10:28.860 --> 10:30.740
O-One more... let's try one more time.

10:38.830 --> 10:39.910
Yamada!

10:40.120 --> 10:40.910
Oh, dear...

10:41.120 --> 10:44.960
By the way, where did you
go for winter break, Ichikawa?

10:45.290 --> 10:46.630
Ah, um...

10:46.920 --> 10:48.730
I just went back to my hometown in Akita.

10:49.300 --> 10:51.130
I got injured there, though.

10:51.470 --> 10:52.590
Akita...

10:53.090 --> 10:53.920
Hmm...

10:54.640 --> 10:56.200
They told me off.

10:56.680 --> 10:58.390
Oh, right, how about you, Yamada?

10:58.810 --> 11:00.490
Where did you go for winter break?

11:00.490 --> 11:03.270
Hm? I didn't go on a trip, but...

11:03.410 --> 11:05.120
I went to Aoyama with Miku,

11:05.120 --> 11:06.880
then spent Christmas Eve with Ichikawa,

11:06.940 --> 11:08.590
welcomed the new year at Nyaa's house,

11:08.590 --> 11:10.070
and did my first shrine visit with...

11:11.820 --> 11:14.370
C-Christmas Eve? Wait... wait a minute.

11:15.030 --> 11:15.620
Huh?

11:16.530 --> 11:19.700
I guess it does make
you think "now hold on"...

11:20.040 --> 11:22.540
Anyway, what about you, Hara?

11:22.750 --> 11:25.730
With Kanzaki,
I only did my first shrine visit...

11:25.730 --> 11:29.920
Huh? I asked you about your winter break,
why are you talking about Kanzaki?

11:29.920 --> 11:32.280
Ack! I got tricked!

11:32.280 --> 11:34.650
Been a while since
it's so warm and fluffy.

11:35.050 --> 11:36.220
So, what happened?

11:39.310 --> 11:40.310
Sorry for the wait!

11:43.390 --> 11:44.120
Um...

11:44.390 --> 11:46.980
Club is on break,
so I tried growing it out.

11:47.320 --> 11:50.000
S-Sideburns, huh...

11:50.400 --> 11:53.050
Um... uhh...

11:53.740 --> 11:56.630
What should I have done in that situation?

11:56.830 --> 12:00.450
I didn't mean to judge
his appearance or anything...

12:00.750 --> 12:05.250
If someone you like does
something that doesn't suit them...

12:09.040 --> 12:12.470
U-Uh, I mean,
I don't really have anyone I like,

12:12.470 --> 12:13.800
so I don't know.

12:14.220 --> 12:16.280
You're still saying that...

12:16.800 --> 12:18.550
You lot over there.

12:18.890 --> 12:21.060
Tuck your bangs under your bandanas.

12:21.390 --> 12:22.980
Oh, okay!

12:25.190 --> 12:27.110
I'll do it for you! Look over here.

12:29.400 --> 12:32.150
J-Just a bit. Let just a bit out.

12:38.450 --> 12:39.840
It looks so weird!

12:44.160 --> 12:46.040
I see...

12:48.670 --> 12:50.040
All done!

12:50.250 --> 12:51.040
What?

12:51.230 --> 12:55.020
This is because you didn't help, Hara!

12:55.020 --> 12:56.360
Sorry about that.

12:56.360 --> 12:57.800
Well, it still tastes fine, I bet!

12:59.490 --> 13:00.800
Let's see...

13:01.260 --> 13:03.310
Oh, that's the one I made!

13:03.560 --> 13:05.080
- Wha...
- Chomp!

13:05.080 --> 13:05.730
Huh?

13:06.370 --> 13:09.210
A-Adachi, yours tastes the best!

13:09.480 --> 13:12.270
Don't you like me too much, man?

13:19.490 --> 13:21.580
Oh, this fell out.

13:22.990 --> 13:25.080
This keychain is so cute!

13:25.890 --> 13:26.500
Yeah!

13:27.330 --> 13:29.080
Akita dogs are so cute!

13:30.590 --> 13:32.420
How nice...

13:33.750 --> 13:36.480
Ah, Hara! Have you eaten already?

13:37.050 --> 13:39.260
I-I'm on a diet, so...

13:39.640 --> 13:42.470
I think you're fine
as you are now, though.

13:42.850 --> 13:44.350
Don't you think so too, Ichikawa?

13:44.510 --> 13:45.850
Huh? Uh...

13:50.020 --> 13:52.900
Then, you shouldn't grow out
your sideburns again, too!

14:00.570 --> 14:02.200
Earlier, Hara...

14:02.870 --> 14:05.620
She must have realized
what's going on, right?

14:06.200 --> 14:07.680
That thing about the akita dog...

14:08.660 --> 14:09.410
All good?

14:09.670 --> 14:11.140
Oh, yeah.

14:11.830 --> 14:15.130
If she asks Yamada about it,
what would she answer with?

14:16.170 --> 14:17.270
Wait, I guess it's fine.

14:17.840 --> 14:20.530
Stuff like that is
normal between girls, right?

14:21.220 --> 14:23.850
Besides, Yamada gets along with everyone.

14:24.140 --> 14:27.560
I bet she gives and
receives a lot of souvenirs...

14:31.190 --> 14:32.270
I-I'm sorry!

14:32.440 --> 14:33.560
I-It's fine.

14:35.860 --> 14:37.690
Sorry I wasn't helpful.

14:38.240 --> 14:39.110
Nah...

14:39.740 --> 14:42.160
Lately, Yamada has been apologizing a lot.

14:43.030 --> 14:44.580
"Don't worry about it too much."

14:45.030 --> 14:47.080
"Just being next to you is fun enough."

14:47.620 --> 14:50.120
I wish I can say something
as frivolous as that.

14:54.250 --> 14:54.880
Here.

14:55.670 --> 14:58.380
My sister had her
coming of age ceremony the other day.

14:59.900 --> 15:01.320
So cute!

15:01.320 --> 15:02.510
Pretty funny, right?

15:03.260 --> 15:05.260
So are you, who has this photo saved!

15:05.360 --> 15:07.260
N-No, that's...

15:09.520 --> 15:10.270
Right!

15:10.770 --> 15:12.770
That photo of the snow scenery
you asked me to take.

15:13.350 --> 15:14.660
Huh? What's that?

15:14.940 --> 15:18.040
Oh, this is when I fell from the tree.

15:18.230 --> 15:19.360
Pretty funny, right?

15:25.800 --> 15:26.720
Ah, no, uh...

15:27.240 --> 15:30.260
Crap! I planned to never say it!

15:31.870 --> 15:33.500
So, that arm...

15:34.170 --> 15:35.730
It's because I asked?

15:35.730 --> 15:37.420
No! This is...

15:38.750 --> 15:41.170
Because... I'm not careful enough.

15:43.680 --> 15:46.800
Oh, speaking of which,
it's forecasted to snow next week.

15:47.820 --> 15:48.970
I couldn't say it.

15:50.180 --> 15:51.980
That when I think of Yamada,

15:52.430 --> 15:54.310
I can't focus on my surroundings.

15:58.520 --> 16:01.860
Oh, right. They say it'll snow next week.

16:02.360 --> 16:04.280
Huh? I said that earlier.

16:04.530 --> 16:07.010
Huh? Oh, right!

16:07.490 --> 16:08.700
I'm sorry.

16:09.990 --> 16:11.540
That face of Yamada's...

16:12.000 --> 16:13.210
That was the first time I had seen it.

16:17.750 --> 16:18.670
Yamada...

16:19.040 --> 16:20.960
She didn't contact me yesterday.

16:21.550 --> 16:24.440
I wonder if she's bothered by my injury...

16:24.800 --> 16:26.590
Hey. Got a moment?

16:28.970 --> 16:30.680
She's acting strange?

16:31.010 --> 16:32.270
Yeah, Yamada.

16:32.560 --> 16:35.140
Yesterday, she only had one fries.

16:35.480 --> 16:36.310
One single fry?

16:36.650 --> 16:37.610
No, one bag.

16:37.980 --> 16:39.690
She usually would finish two
with room to spare.

16:40.190 --> 16:42.690
Icchi, you have an inkling of anything?

16:42.990 --> 16:43.820
I'm not sure...

16:44.240 --> 16:45.360
Why are you asking me?

16:45.740 --> 16:48.240
That's true. Why are we asking Ichikawa?

16:48.620 --> 16:50.410
- But, you know...
- Morning.

16:51.310 --> 16:52.970
Hm? What's wrong?

16:53.290 --> 16:54.010
Nothin'.

17:04.010 --> 17:05.840
She really is bothered by it...

17:06.170 --> 17:08.260
That she caused my injury.

17:10.010 --> 17:10.850
Huh?

17:11.820 --> 17:12.460
It's not here.

17:14.220 --> 17:15.770
Akita Kentaro isn't here.

17:16.100 --> 17:17.600
- Who?
- No, uh...

17:18.940 --> 17:19.870
It's nothing.

17:22.020 --> 17:23.530
Was it there when you left your house?

17:24.650 --> 17:26.050
It might not had been.

17:26.150 --> 17:28.990
So it might be at home, I think.

17:30.370 --> 17:32.240
Everyone, take your seats!

17:35.890 --> 17:38.810
What should I say at a time like this?

17:39.790 --> 17:42.810
I shouldn't say I'll give her my Kenjiro.

17:46.260 --> 17:49.260
The forecast said the snow's
going to get heavier today,

17:49.340 --> 17:52.150
so we'll end classes here
and you all can go home.

17:52.150 --> 17:53.600
- Really?!
- Alright!

17:59.060 --> 18:02.320
Seems like Hara lost a dog keychain.

18:02.520 --> 18:03.320
A dog keychain?

18:05.070 --> 18:07.780
Akita Kentarou is about that thing, right?

18:08.150 --> 18:10.700
Yamada looked really sad...

18:11.070 --> 18:11.820
What?

18:13.410 --> 18:15.080
Thank you. That's enough.

18:16.540 --> 18:17.750
I'll look for it.

18:22.790 --> 18:24.810
Dammit... dammit, dammit!

18:25.130 --> 18:26.630
Dammit, dammit, dammit!

18:27.590 --> 18:30.480
Then again, the scope is way too wide...

18:30.930 --> 18:34.430
I don't even know her path to school.

18:42.830 --> 18:44.120
Looking for something?

18:44.400 --> 18:45.980
Huh? Not really.

18:46.820 --> 18:49.590
Anna doesn't go this way often.

18:50.070 --> 18:51.610
Her house is over there.

18:52.070 --> 18:53.910
That's the path she usually takes.

18:55.370 --> 18:56.240
Thank you.

19:06.710 --> 19:07.880
My body is freezing...

19:08.510 --> 19:10.400
My arm that got fractured hurt.

19:11.720 --> 19:13.720
This thing... is meaningless.

19:14.800 --> 19:16.350
It's only for my own satisfaction.

19:19.180 --> 19:20.020
But...

19:20.490 --> 19:22.350
("We...")

19:33.590 --> 19:35.740
("...Are Searching")

19:35.740 --> 19:37.950
(Ichikawa's looking for something)
(What... Thank you)

19:45.840 --> 19:47.380
He's not at home, either.

19:48.130 --> 19:49.460
I couldn't find him anywhere.

19:51.210 --> 19:53.610
Even after I looked, and looked...

19:53.720 --> 19:54.340
He's still here!

19:57.100 --> 19:58.310
I'm sure he is.

20:00.430 --> 20:02.430
Even if we can't find him,
he's here somewhere.

20:02.770 --> 20:03.850
He won't disappear.

20:04.480 --> 20:05.270
So...

20:06.120 --> 20:07.330
...don't worry about it.

20:21.580 --> 20:23.250
There he is... there he is!

20:24.500 --> 20:26.670
The person who found it
hung it on the tree!

20:29.880 --> 20:31.010
Thank you...

20:35.300 --> 20:36.590
Thank you so much.

20:37.490 --> 20:40.390
Had... Had I not met you here,

20:40.810 --> 20:42.030
I wouldn't have looked up.

21:01.330 --> 21:02.260
Atchoo!

21:02.410 --> 21:03.700
Oh, are you okay?

21:04.040 --> 21:05.750
I just never learn...

21:10.670 --> 21:11.500
My house...

21:14.010 --> 21:15.760
...is right over there.

21:17.130 --> 21:18.300
You wanna...

21:19.100 --> 21:20.390
...warm up for a bit?

21:30.520 --> 21:32.980
(Karte 13: "We Are Searching")
